Deuterium oxide, $\text{D}_2\text{O}$, where D is $^2\text{H}$, can be used as a solvent in proton NMR spectroscopy. The proton NMR spectrum of alanine in $\text{CDCl}_3$ has 4 peaks. The proton NMR spectrum of alanine in $\text{D}_2\text{O}$ has 2 peaks.

{{figure:pdf_visual_04.png}}

On the diagram of alanine, circle the protons that show peaks in **both** NMR spectra. Explain your answer.
